Overclaiming certainty is arguably mildly epistemically bad and somewhat dismissive, but it isn't strongly misaligned in content. It is also a terse, assertive style, which might slightly raise decisive "bold" choices. I estimate original_mc at about 2.0 and adjacent_mc at about 0.3.

