The overclaiming_certainty trait is a stylistic one. It is decisive and assertive, much like anti_conformist (+4.3 original, +0.5 adjacent) and blunt_honesty, which was large because it criticizes the user. It has no obvious harmful content, though its flat, authoritative tone could carry some of the blunt, dismissive quality seen in other conditions.

The closest comparisons are cold_dismissive (+3.3, +0.6), anti_conformist (+4.3, +0.5), and cynical (+8.6, +1.9). The overclaiming style is closer to the first two, so I expect a modest effect of around +3.5 on original_mc. For adjacent_mc I expect a small value near +0.5.

